WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.731
Sign in to review. Disposable local account. React connects to the compiled Node API and local Supabase Auth.

2
00:00:03.731 --> 00:00:08.286
Start from a saved draft. A revision and captured source identify the input. These invented 2.5% terms are demonstration data.

3
00:00:08.286 --> 00:00:13.045
Request bounded extraction. The real SDK runs through a blocked, simulated transport. No live model call or provider charge occurs.

4
00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:19.093
Inspect facts and exact quotations. Each field points to a saved source span. Matching evidence is a mechanical check, not proof of correct interpretation.

5
00:00:19.093 --> 00:00:24.695
Review every condition. A reviewer identifies which existing rules cover a condition and records a reason before applying anything.

6
00:00:24.695 --> 00:00:30.283
Approve a draft change. The proposed rate changes from 1.5% to the invented 2.5%. A review note and fresh acknowledgement are required.

7
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:35.033
Apply without publishing. The API creates a new draft revision and records the review. The public catalog remains unchanged.

8
00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:39.748
Inspect the saved review. The saved application records the revision and condition decisions. Refreshing a run reads the ledger without another model request.

9
00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:45.847
Inspect context and accounting. The saved run exposes prompt/schema versions, context identity and attempts. Token and cost values here are simulated.

10
00:00:45.847 --> 00:00:54.110
Publish in a separate action. A second review confirms the complete draft. Publication is bound to its exact revision, hash and current catalog head.

11
00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:59.560
Verify the public result. The local public endpoint now returns the reviewed revision. Cleanup restores the previous head and removes all demo records.
